node_modules/
# The release asset is a copy of index.html built by tools/release.sh. The other releases did not track theirs,
# and a stale copy of the game in the tree is a file that can be mistaken for the game.
wake-*.html

# AND THE OTHER THING A TOOL WRITES. `path-search.js` regenerates `wake-reachable.txt` on every run - the sorted list
# of scenes it reached - and it was showing up as untracked noise after every search. Same reason as the line above,
# one member short: A FILE A TOOL WRITES IS NOT A FILE THE REPOSITORY KEEPS, and leaving it untracked means every run
# leaves the tree dirty for whoever looks next.
wake-reachable.txt
